going to begin with this you'll be very  interested in this as a new mom  the u.s is one of the world's only  developed countries that does not  guarantee  paid family leave think about that for  just a second nearly one in four mothers  in this country  returns to work within two weeks of  giving birth president biden's paid  leave proposal in the american family's  plan would provide  12 weeks of paid leave to workers caring  for a new children  or a sick family member tech  entrepreneur alexis ohanian is a long  time advocate for paid family leave  ohanian is founder of the investment  fund 776  he's a co-founder of reddit and of  course he's a husband of tennis star  serena williams  and best of all he's a father of  three-year-old olympia one of the cutest  little girls in the world  alexis hey it's so good to see you again  good to be back i know this issue hits  very close to home because  i remember reading a story that you  wrote that when you were born and you're  an only child  your dad took off one day from work just  one  and when olympia was born how much time  did you take off from work  i took my full leave you know 12 weeks  and  and at the time i wanted to set an  example as a leader of my company and a  leader in the tech industry i wanted to  role model  the kind of behavior i wanted my  employees uh to  follow especially men um and  you know i was grateful um to have that  responsibility or have that opportunity  and that responsibility  because it was you know a very  complicated child birth for my wife  yes we remember reading about documented  yes but you know the thing that's  interesting alexis  you hadn't even thought about this issue  until you had your own child  i know sad but true um you know credit  to our  vp of people and culture caitlyn  holloway she was the one who had brought  the proposal the plan  to the company and you know i was i was  really just checking a box because it  seemed like this was something we would  just need to have in order to get the  best  and the brightest to come work for us um  but it wasn't until it really  deeply and personally affected me that i  realized this is something that  every american deserves to have uh and  and feel confident to take advantage of  and i'm  thrilled to see what president biden has  laid down here  i agree with you luckily you got to  spend so much time with olympia  what are some of the priceless  milestones that you feel like you got to  see if you and because you were there  i mean i you know just spending the time  that i got to spend early on  i had never grown up around babies so  changing diapers  doing all these things were were pivotal  and it was it was important you know  serena was coming out of  a number of surgeries and those  responsibilities just sort of naturally  fell on papa and just getting that time  even  even the slightly loopy late nights  trying to to sort of calm her back to  sleep  were moments that i'm grateful i got to  spend because i think they laid a  foundation  for for me to know look there's a lot of  stuff you just learn on the fly as a  parent  and going through that period and having  the time to just learn on the go and  improvise and actually  feel like it's going to work out gave me  the confidence to know no matter what  i can be there for her i can figure it  out we'll get through it  and i'm grateful for it and every dad  deserves it just like every mom yeah  alexis says it's anthony as much as it's  the right thing to do  it sure seems like you also say it's  actually good for the economy  explain that yes look i'm coming at this  as a business leader  i'm saying this is vital because i want  my employees to be  working when they're at work i want them  to be their whole selves i want them to  be focused  and if you have a newborn certainly if  you have a situation with complications  or extra stress  you're not going to be your best self at  work and the idea that this is a country  that  believes in families is the bedrock  which i believe it does  but also as a country where one in four  american women is back to work  10 days after giving birth i can't  reconcile those things  and i want to know it's possible for  everyone because i know it's better for  the health outcomes of  the the mother of the children and that  means cost reduction  that means cost savings that means more  prosperity for all of us  and uh and i think it's actually on the  horizon now and as an employer i'm  excited because i want this to be  something that's not just a privilege  for the few to be able to take but  something for every american yeah i  agree with you you sent a very powerful  message  last year when you resigned from your  board of directors and you you said  you want to give your seat to a person  of color what role did fatherhood play  in that decision at the time because at  the time people thought whoa  you could have just added another seat  to your board you could have done that  well you know it was it was thinking  about a future conversation i'd have  with olympia  and knowing that she's going to grow up  with  a a very different very different  uh situation uh than i did and  as a father of a daughter especially a  black daughter  i wanted to make sure i'd have really  good answers for her about decisions i  made in my career and my work  and one of the things i realized even in  that active resignation was  it was a forcing function to bring  change not just  to be replaced by a black director but  also to finally ban  you know a number of hate communities on  the platform and so that was  you know it was it was motivating for me  because so much of what i've tried to do  especially in the last year since  is set an example and do the kind of  work that i hope when  you know she's a snarky teenager she can  look back on and say all right you know  what  my father used the platform he had he  used the privilege he had to  to make things better for me and a lot  of people like me yeah you have a lot  going on  you also have a podcast called business  dad  wow um and you also you're talking to  high profile dads about business and  balance that work life  what have you learned from those fathers  you know  um one of my favorite guests was hassan  minaj  and and one of the things he talked  about you know his wife called him out  specifically for this early on and said  take this time with your daughter take  this time to be with her  because you will never get it back and  and that will be something you'll look  back  on uh as a regret and and he he you know  he's also a hard working  you know uh uh pretty motivated uh  career-driven talented young man  now alexis you've been called up by your  wife too which which i also  i rather enjoy i remember serena well i  remember  serena serena said to you you work  harder than i do and you said thank you  so much she said  that is not a compliment that's such a  good way to put it because she works  very hard she goes that's not a  compliment  dude that you work harder than i do what  message was she saying to you  what she hit on the head was the fact  that i had a kind of warped view  of of the path to excellence and the  path to greatness being a direct result  of just pure  work and that is obviously core to it  but  one thing that i'm still working on is  is balancing that with time off with  time away with time to reset and  recharge  and something she's really good at is  shutting it off and focusing on  family time or personal time and and you  know i'm always a smartphone away  from dipping back into a term sheet or  dipping back into work and  yeah i certainly uh certainly still get  checked from time to time on that one  because it's  it's something that i i want to be my  best i think we all do and that was  i think one of the motivations behind  even starting business dad  we need more men talking about this  stuff exactly because  i mean so many career-driven men who  also  as soon as you get them talking about  their kids you realize they care as much  about this they care more about this  exactly alexis ohanian alexis ohanian  we've been debating how do you say your  last name  i  okay alexis thank you very much we  appreciate it thank you so much

